	<uuid uuid="{64568fea-a2d0-54b4-bf3d-8aa10dddc076}" />
	<names>
		<name lang="en">EL9100 potential feed terminal, description view</name>
		<name lang="fr">EL9100 borne d'alimentation de potentiel, vue réaliste</name>
	</names>
	<elementInformations>
		<elementInformation name="manufacturer" show="1">Beckhoff</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="manufacturer_reference" show="1">EL9100</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="designation" show="1">EtherCAT Terminal, labels as drawn</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="description" show="1">EtherCAT Terminal, potential feed terminal. Pin names are the Beckhoff terminal points in the order of the user's own drawing (left column 1 to 4, right column 5 to 8): 1 END1, 2 NC1, 3 NC3, 4 NC5, 5 END2, 6 NC2, 7 NC4, 8 NC6. The channel is the signal in the I/O table, not the pin number. Check this against the datasheet of your terminal.</elementInformation>
	</elementInformations>
	<informations>Author: QElectroTech contributors
Description view made by misc/beckhoff/gen_description.py from the realistic view: legends, LEDs and power contacts are generic, check them against the datasheet. License: see http://qelectrotech.org/wiki/doc/elements_license</informations>
